INSERT INTO "assistant_chat_sessions" ("id", "session_id", "user_id", "user_role", "department_id", "title", "page_context_json", "messages_json", "created_at", "updated_at") VALUES (1, 'test_session_integ_1788663563', 4, 'HoD', 2, 'Chat Session with HOD Test', '{"current_path": "/hod/assessments/active", "page_title": "Active Department Assessments - NASC Portal", "metrics_summary": {"total_active": "4 Exams Live", "overall_pass_rate": "87.4%", "department": "Computer Applications"}, "visible_tables": [{"caption": "Live Assessments Table", "headers": ["Assessment ID", "Course", "Enrolled", "Submitted", "Pass %"], "rows": [["ASM-101", "Python Programming", "45", "42", "92%"], ["ASM-102", "Database Management", "38", "35", "84%"], ["ASM-103", "Data Structures", "50", "20", "In Progress"]]}], "quick_links": ["Analytics (/hod/analytics)", "Approvals (/hod/approvals)"]}'::jsonb, '[{"id": "welcome_init", "sender": "assistant", "text": "**Welcome, HOD Test!**\n\nI am your **NASC AI Assistant**, live-aware of your active screen and department data. How may I assist you today?", "timestamp": "08:29:23"}, {"id": "user_1788663563902", "sender": "user", "text": "What does the visible table show about ASM-101 and ASM-103?", "timestamp": "08:29:23", "tools_executed": []}, {"id": "assistant_1788663569105", "sender": "assistant", "text": "**Analyzing Assessment Data**\n\nI''m currently focused on analyzing the user''s request for `ASM-101` and `ASM-103`, as observed on the screen within the `Active Department Assessments` context. I see metrics for \"Computer Applications,\" but must prioritize `Computer Science` due to strict tenancy, so will handle as a conflict and clarify the department focus. The screen displays active assessments, and I''m correlating those details with the available assessment IDs from the table data to provide relevant data in context.\n\n\n**Interpreting Assessment Requests**\n\nI''m now zeroing in on the specific assessments, `ASM-101` and `ASM-103`. The screen''s data shows the department as \"Computer Applications\", but I''m adhering to the \"Computer Science\" tenancy. So, I need to account for this conflict. I''m noting the course details for each assessment, and enrollment numbers. I have \"Python Programming\" for ASM-101 (92% pass rate) and \"Data Structures\" for ASM-103, which is in progress. I''m working to reconcile the conflicting department data on the screen with the department tenancy rule.", "timestamp": "08:29:29", "tools_executed": []}]'::jsonb, '2026-09-06 08:29:23.886479', '2026-09-06 08:29:29.105298') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "assistant_chat_sessions" ("id", "session_id", "user_id", "user_role", "department_id", "title", "page_context_json", "messages_json", "created_at", "updated_at") VALUES (3, 'sess_1_1788683231', 1, 'Administrator', NULL, 'Chat Session with System Administrator', '{"current_path": "/", "page_title": "Nehru Arts and Science College (Autonomous)NASC", "active_tab": "", "metrics_summary": {}, "visible_tables": [], "quick_links": []}'::jsonb, '[{"id": "welcome_init", "sender": "assistant", "text": "**Welcome, System Administrator!**\n\nI am your **NASC AI Assistant**, live-aware of your active screen and department data. How may I assist you today?", "timestamp": "08:35:39"}, {"id": "user_1788663941203", "sender": "user", "text": "Show me the latest department KPIs, pass percentages, and average scores.", "timestamp": "08:35:41", "tools_executed": []}, {"id": "assistant_1788663953953", "sender": "assistant", "text": "**Analyzing Department KPIs**\n\nI''m currently focused on identifying the most efficient way to fulfill the user''s request for department KPIs. The `get_department_kpis` tool appears to be the most relevant, especially since it specifies \"pass percentage, average test scores, total attempts, and competency performance\". Considering the user''s scope (\"System Administrator\"), I need to determine the scope of departments the tool can provide. Since \"department KPIs\" is plural, I will assume a request for an overview is in scope. I will start by calling the tool for specific example department codes, such as ''CSE''.\n\n\n**Refining KPI Retrieval**\n\nI''ve re-evaluated the tool selection; `get_department_kpis` remains the focus. While the request is for \"latest department KPIs,\" I realize the tool only accepts a single department code. The System Administrator scope implies a need for a broader overview, so I''ll generate a comprehensive view by calling the tool iteratively for a few key departments: ''CSE'', ''IT'', and ''AI-DS''. This approach aims to deliver the requested information effectively, given the tool''s limitations.\n\n\n**Investigating Data Anomalies**\n\nThe \"CSE\" department call yielded no results, which is concerning. I''ve shifted focus to alternative departments like \"IT\" and \"AI-DS\" to address the user''s request for department KPIs. Hoping this adjustment will resolve the empty dataset.\n\n\n**Investigating Call Issues**\n\nI''ve hit a snag. The initial call for ''IT'' yielded an empty list. This outcome echoes the ''IT'' attempt, which also returned nothing. I am now proceeding by trying ''AI-DS'' to see if this affects the list. I suspect the issue might be with the invocation method.\n\n\n**Investigating Alternate KPIs**\n\nI''ve hit a roadblock with the specific department calls, as they''re consistently returning empty results. I suspect there might be an issue with how I''m calling `get_department_kpis` or perhaps it''s temporarily unavailable. Given my scope, I''m now exploring broader tools, like `get_live_exam_status`, `get_question_bank_summary`, `get_pending_approvals`, and `get_at_risk_students`, hoping to find a workaround. However, none directly offer the KPIs I need. I''ll need to report the current limitations.\n\n\n**Reporting Limitations**\n\nI am now certain that direct retrieval of specific department KPIs, including pass percentages and average scores, is unavailable at this time. The `get_department_kpis` tool consistently returned empty results, suggesting a backend issue or a misconfiguration in how the calls are being made. I will inform the user of these limitations.", "timestamp": "08:35:53", "tools_executed": [{"tool": "get_department_kpis", "arguments": {"department_code_or_name": "CSE"}, "result": {"departments": [], "evaluated_at": "2026-09-06 08:35:45 UTC"}}, {"tool": "get_department_kpis", "arguments": {"department_code_or_name": "IT"}, "result": {"departments": [], "evaluated_at": "2026-09-06 08:35:46 UTC"}}, {"tool": "get_department_kpis", "arguments": {"department_code_or_name": "AI-DS"}, "result": {"departments": [], "evaluated_at": "2026-09-06 08:35:49 UTC"}}]}, {"id": "user_1788664006520", "sender": "user", "text": "What is the current live status of ongoing exams and active students in the portal?", "timestamp": "08:36:46", "tools_executed": []}, {"id": "user_1788664063022", "sender": "user", "text": "Are there any student assessment activation requests pending HoD approval?", "timestamp": "08:37:43", "tools_executed": []}, {"id": "user_1788664064315", "sender": "user", "text": "Are there any student assessment activation requests pending HoD approval?", "timestamp": "08:37:44", "tools_executed": []}, {"id": "user_1788664067229", "sender": "user", "text": "Identify at-risk students who scored below 50% in recent assessment rounds.", "timestamp": "08:37:47", "tools_executed": []}, {"id": "user_1788664084986", "sender": "user", "text": "Identify at-risk students who scored below 50% in recent assessment rounds.", "timestamp": "08:38:04", "tools_executed": []}, {"id": "assistant_1788664091160", "sender": "assistant", "text": "**Pinpointing At-Risk Students**\n\nI''ve determined that the `get_at_risk_students` tool is the most appropriate for this task. My current approach involves configuring it to specifically target students who scored below 50%. I plan to set the `score_threshold` parameter to 50.0 and will rely on the default `limit` parameter. The current screen context is irrelevant to this specific action. I''m now ready to call the tool with the specified parameters.", "timestamp": "08:38:11", "tools_executed": [{"tool": "get_at_risk_students", "arguments": {"score_threshold": 50}, "result": {"score_threshold_checked": 50.0, "flagged_candidate_count": 0, "at_risk_students": []}}]}, {"id": "user_1788664762407", "sender": "user", "text": "Identify at-risk students who scored below 50% in recent assessment rounds.", "timestamp": "08:49:22", "tools_executed": []}, {"id": "assistant_1788664766